    "turn_idx": 19,
    "turn_text": "And so my next point was going to be. The way we do that isn't by spending exorbitant amounts of money attracting those businesses here. It's not a regulatory race to the bottom. It's not any of the ways that I think conservatives oftentimes think you attract businesses. The way you attract jobs is to attract the workforce. And the way to attract the workforce is to say, you come to Delaware, we're gonna have a livable minimum wage. We're gonna have paid family and medical leave. We are going to pass Medicaid buy-in so that you've got an affordable option on the individual marketplace. We're gonna protect workers in the gig economy. We're gonna lower the cost of housing, and we're gonna make affordable housing a reality for every single person. These are the ways that you attract young people to this state. It's not attracting businesses here. If you build it, they will come. If you attract the workforce, the businesses will come. The way to attract the workforce is pro-working family policies. And I think as millennials, a lot of times people think the way we attract millennials is we build cool shit, right? We have great parks and clean streets, and those might be parts of it. But at the end of the day, millennials are looking for the kinds of policies that allow them to start a family. be able to not just survive, but thrive. And that means those pro-working family policies. So my point is that if you take the argument that they're making in the language that's being made that has kept taxes relatively low here in Delaware, particularly property taxes, When you take those arguments and you say, I accept the premise that we need to be smart about our economic growth. But the path forward there is innovative progressive policies. And so I think you can meet people where they are, use the language that they use to make a point that they might not otherwise hear if it's not if you're not meeting them where they are. And so I think that's, for me, I don't think you could, I don't think you sacrifice your values or your positions. by accepting some language that allows people to hear the message and understand it from whatever perspective they're coming from because in a democracy you have to build a majoritarian coalition and inevitably that coalition will include people who are coming to the issue from a different perspective and it might be a perspective that you disagree with even fundamentally.",
