    "turn_text": "Yeah, I mean, obviously no one's going to make an overture towards me because I'm just a moron and a small studio here. But so it's hypothetical as far as I know. But I do know that there is, to me, the way I've been framing it is that there's this sort of You know, there's certainly, you know, freshmen who are coming in with the understanding that they are sort of the vanguard of a progressive sort of socialist leftist movement and others who maybe could be part of that. And that coalition, I think, is going to be the one that could create the most change. Like I said, I'm I think that the time is right. The General Assembly has changed in ways that really could make people sort of look forward to something like that. I'm not sanguine because I'm just a cynical, pessimistic person. But I do think that Because of the situation going into this general assembly, that people do have an expectation that some accomplishments are going to have to be had for people to be able to say, yeah, thanks for voting in a new group of fairly younger, more progressive members. And so I don't know how that's going to pan out, actually, but I'm interested to see.",
