    "episode_id": 92312,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92312.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 29,
    "turn_text": "I've said the same, the same just being here. I mean, this is the second time that we've spoken and recorded it the first time was here. And now it's like this. And so I've, we've Carl and I have talked, you know, we've done about half and half, half in person and half on Zoom. And yeah, there is a trade off. I mean, I certainly like the flexibility of Zoom. We've been able to have different types of guests, panels, different things, which have been cool. But the feel of it is different. And so yeah, there's pros and cons to it. And yeah, I mean, my personal feeling is that as far as any kind of activist pressure, that really can only be done in person. There's something there about sort of pressuring somebody face to face that's going to do something that a virtual interaction is not going to do. It certainly allows people the opportunity to get more involved and to watch what's happening, to see what people say, to see how things work, and that could turn out to be a game changer. I don't know. I guess it really depends on what kind of stuff goes down and over and how meaningful it is to people's lives. And so getting into that, let's talk about sort of priorities. You listed off four or five of them, and I think they're all great. Some of them that you didn't mention that I know will come up are, I guess, marijuana legalization, full legalization. I don't know where you put that on your priorities and also some of the gun issues. My personal feeling is sort of mixed on that. A lot of people know my position on guns in general. I put that very low on my priorities, but I also understand that there's been organizing an activism around this already. And so, you know, when people are involved and they're telling you that this is something that they want, that has to be taken into account. I mean, that's just a fact. So how do you prioritize some of the things you mentioned, some of the things I've mentioned and what do you think are the other than just your priorities, some of the other influences on what could possibly get done and what might not.",
