    "turn_text": "going to test drivers? I don't know. We don't test drivers when the doctor prescribes them muscle relaxers or OxyContin or anything else. There's no test for that. People are driving all around on that. Nobody cares. People care, but these are silly arguments. But the good thing is we already know the arguments we're going to run up against and the people who are going to make these arguments. So the question really becomes, do we think we have the acumen and the coalition building and the strategic thinking on priorities to achieve those things. What do you think is different today than when the $15 minimum wage failed last time? For example, I'll use that as an example because that's one that pretty spectacularly, people still talk about that failure in the training wage and that type of thing. What are some of the strategic things we're going to try to do to overcome some of these Just some of the opposition that you've seen over the past two or three years.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
