    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92312.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 34,
    "turn_text": "I think there are a couple things that create greater possibility. One again is the economic crisis and the public health crisis. I really do think that has fundamentally changed the public's improved, I should say, the public's appetite for meaningful economic reforms. I think similarly it's also improved the appetite for for members for elected officials. I think, you know, you've raised this. We've talked about a number of times. I think the influx of new folks has over the last two years. But I think in particular, the influx of new folks and the way they were elected this year creates a new, more significant opening. You know, I also think, look, I think that the leadership, I'm really, I've obviously never served under a different leadership team, but I am really excited about the leadership team that we have in the Senate. I think that I have in the Senate that they are three leaders who understand the opportunities to do big things, the responsibility to do big things, that good policy is good politics. And I think our eager to see all of us, as they say, change the world. I mean, they've literally said, let's go spread our wings and change the world. And so I think there's a number of things that have happened in the last six months that create a, I think, again, not a route to shore success. but certainly an increased possibility for passage of all of the issues we've talked about that's much higher than it's ever been in the past.",
