    "turn_text": "in it. But my sense is that there is real appetite across the caucus and across the chamber. And, and I haven't spoken to every single person. I, you know, I haven't been able to take a vote count or whip count make a whip count on on on these issues. You know, hard whip count on these on a lot of these issues. I know people are. But my sense is that. is that people across the sort of ideological span of the caucuses are there and are ready and are allies. And that doesn't mean that there aren't barriers. That doesn't mean people, those coalitions will shift depending on the issue itself. But I don't think it's just the folks that are the ones that you mentioned. I think that there is real appetite across the span of each caucus.",
