  {
    "episode_id": 92312,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92312.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 41,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, I think What I'm going to be watching the most is, yeah, just the machinations. If it's more of the same, and I don't mean the same, you know, people necessarily, it's not, or the same arguments, it won't be because there is a desire for things to move. But I wonder if we see the same roadblocks in the house, for example. where where things that's that's sort of a wild card i think uh... i i i assume people have been thinking about that because there wasn't leadership changes in the house uh... i i think a lot of a lot of folks you know you mentioned changes to the law enforcement officers bill of rights uh... i i know that the the the house at least the house leadership is not going to be keen on those i don't think And so I'm really interested to see what kind of battle lines are drawn because it really is time for, you know, it's time for new arguments and new action. And I wonder whether people are just going to, how that's going to shake out. That's the interesting part sort of to me. And through that shakeout, I hope that some of this stuff can, you know, we can see some big victories. One or two that we can hang our hat on and say see that's because I guess my feeling and you sort of mentioned this before and maybe Your situation is a little bit different But because so many Challengers did win in this last election I think they're going to be put to the test. And if they're not able to point to some victory or some change, I think it's going to be very difficult to continue on this road and convince people that stepping out of their comfort zone or stepping out of capitalism and that bubble start stepping out and trying to be more imaginative about how we can build Delaware back up after COVID, or how we can get the schools up, you know, change the way we do education that we haven't done in 80 years. Like, if we can't show results, it's going to be very hard to go back out and say let's do this again and again and again and so that's really that's my main goal or concern with all of this is to be able to strategize to bring some results and say yes this this program that we're on this progressive program that's a little more that the challenges the status quo that doesn't play you know by the we don't we you know, the way I always explain it to people is, yeah, you have rules or you have the way I think I don't follow those rules. I don't think that that's the right way. I don't think everyone's agreed that that's how we should proceed. It's very hard to sell that without some victories to point to. So that's what I'm sort of holding out for that.",
